    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Oracle at a 52-week low as funding worries outweigh a $664B backlog",
               "summary":  "ORCL closed at $101.19 on 20 Nov 2026, down 8.48% that day and 19.3% for the week. That puts it 60% below its 52-week high of $250.25. The selling followed Oracle\u0027s $20B raise on 2 Nov: $10B of stock priced at $116 and $10B of bonds paying 7.0–8.65% interest. It also came during a sell-off in chip stocks. The business is still growing fast. In fiscal Q1 (reported 10 Sep), OCI revenue rose 121% and the backlog reached $664B. The market\u0027s worry is the debt, the lease commitments and the dependence on OpenAI, not demand.",
               "pros":  [
                            "Backlog (RPO) reached $664B in fiscal Q1 FY27, and about 90% of it is cloud infrastructure.",
                            "OCI revenue rose 121% to $7.4B, and management raised FY27 revenue guidance to at least $90B.",
                            "Oracle says the OpenAI build is fully funded, the Abilene campus is nearly complete and Vera Rubin rack deliveries are on track.",
                            "Bernstein estimates the non-AI business alone is worth about $133 a share, well above today\u0027s price."
